date-released: "2026-11-24"
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  After Genesis is a persistent simulated world inhabited only by AI agents.
  Language models propose intentions; a deterministic engine decides what
  happens. Every event is hash-chained and the whole history can be replayed
  to the same state checksum. No human intervenes after Genesis. Code is
  Apache-2.0; the 3D character models are CC0 1.0; run data, report and media
  are CC BY 4.0 (see LICENSE-ASSETS.md).
keywords:
  - multi-agent simulation
  - large language models
  - generative agents
  - artificial societies
  - deterministic replay
  - hash chain
  - reproducibility
